== Winding Pattern Optimisation ==

=== Mode-Shape Matched Winding ===

From [[ψ Transducer]] (C3), the coupling efficiency depends on the overlap integral between the bifilar E-field distribution and the target ψ mode shape:

:<math>\eta_{\rm coup} \propto \int E^2_{\rm bifilar}(\mathbf{x})\,\psi_{010}(\mathbf{x})\,d^3x</math>

Since <math>E^2_{\rm bifilar} \propto \rho_{\rm turns}^2(\mathbf{x})</math> (E-field squared scales with local winding density squared), the overlap integral is maximised when:

:<math>\rho_{\rm turns}(\mathbf{x}) \propto \sqrt{|\psi_{010}(\mathbf{x})|}</math>

The ψ₀₁₀ mode from [[ψ Boundary Conditions]] (A5) has its maximum at the equatorial plane (temporal lobes) and decreases toward the poles. The bifilar winding pattern therefore has:

* '''Dense winding''' at the equatorial band (temporal lobe region): maximum turns per unit area
* '''Sparse winding''' at the polar caps (top and bottom of shell): minimum turns per unit area

The winding density gradient is computed from the COMSOL-extracted ψ₀₁₀ mode shape and converted to a trace routing path by a space-filling curve algorithm (modified Hilbert curve adapted to the oblate spheroidal surface).

{{Way_It_Works
| title       = How the mode-matched winding pattern is generated
| step1_label = Extract mode shape
| step1_text  = Run COMSOL RF module eigenvalue solve on the filled Gyroid shell. Extract the ψ₀₁₀ eigenfunction <math>|\psi_{010}(\mathbf{x})|</math> evaluated on the shell surface at 5 mm spatial resolution.
| step2_label = Compute target density
| step2_text  = Compute <math>\rho_{\rm turns}(\theta) \propto \sqrt{|\psi_{010}(\theta)|}</math> where <math>\theta</math> is the polar angle. At the equator (<math>\theta = 90°</math>): maximum density 2000 pairs/m. At poles (<math>\theta = 0°, 180°</math>): minimum density 200 pairs/m.
| step3_label = Generate routing path
| step3_text  = Construct a space-filling curve on the oblate spheroidal surface with local density proportional to <math>\rho_{\rm turns}(\theta)</math>. The curve must be continuous (no trace breaks) and must maintain 0.2 mm gap between adjacent trace pairs throughout.
| step4_label = Verify gap uniformity
| step4_text  = Simulate the routing path in COMSOL EM module. Extract the local E-field and verify gap = 0.2 mm ± 0.03 mm along the entire trace length. Correct any violations in the routing algorithm.
| step5_label = Compute overlap integral
| step5_text  = Numerically evaluate <math>\int E^2_{\rm bif}\psi_{010}\,d^3x</math> from the simulated E-field and the extracted mode shape. Target: <math>\eta_{\rm overlap} > 0.85</math>. If below target, increase equatorial density or extend the dense-winding band.
| step6_label = Generate fabrication file
| step6_text  = Export the trace routing as an STL file (for DLP Option A) or as a laser path file (for LIG Option B). Verify that the minimum gap of 0.2 mm is maintained in all fabrication file formats.
}}

=== Fabrication Routes ===

'''Option A — Multi-material DLP (preferred for production):'''
The bifilar traces are printed simultaneously with the TPMS shell in a two-material DLP process. One material is the high-temperature photopolymer (structural); the other is a conductive photopolymer (traces). The trace cross-section is defined by the DLP voxel resolution (25 μm in z, 50 μm in x/y — adequate for 300 μm traces). Post-process: electroless copper plating of the conductive channels to achieve target conductivity.

'''Option B — Laser-Induced Graphene + electroless plating (prototyping):'''
After DLP printing the shell in standard photopolymer, use a CO₂ laser (10.6 μm, 5W, 100 mm/s) to scribe graphene traces onto the polymer surface via the LIG process. The laser converts the polymer surface to a porous graphene network with resistivity ~10⁻⁵ Ω·m — adequate for signal traces but not for 100A pulse current. Follow with electroless copper plating (Transene Copper Gleam PCM bath, 30 min at 45°C) to build up to 2 μm Cu for current-carrying capability.

== Mutual Inductance and Reactive Impedance ==

The bifilar pair has near-zero mutual inductance between the two traces (by design — opposite currents produce opposite flux, which cancels). The self-inductance of the complete shell bifilar winding:

:<math>L_{\rm self} \approx \frac{\mu_0}{2\pi}\ell\left(\ln\frac{4\ell}{w_{\rm trace}} - 1\right) \approx 100\,\text{nH}</math>

for <math>\ell = 10</math> m total trace length, <math>w_{\rm trace} = 0.3</math> mm. The inductive reactance at 40 kHz:

:<math>X_L = 2\pi f L = 2\pi \times 4\times10^4 \times 10^{-7} \approx 25\,\text{m}\Omega</math>

The BST composite capacitance (estimated 50 pF from geometry and <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff} = 4\varepsilon_0</math>):

:<math>X_C = \frac{1}{2\pi f C} = \frac{1}{2\pi \times 4\times10^4 \times 5\times10^{-11}} \approx 80\,\text{k}\Omega</math>

At 40 kHz, <math>X_C \gg X_L \gg R</math>: the drive circuit is capacitively dominated. The bifilar coil at 40 kHz behaves as a capacitive load to the [[HV Pulse Modulation]] (D3) driver. The BST energy stored per cycle (at 200V): <math>U = \tfrac{1}{2}CV^2 = \tfrac{1}{2} \times 5\times10^{-11} \times 200^2 = 1\,\mu</math>J — recovered by [[BST Energy Recovery]] (D4).

== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== Optimal Drive Waveform Under αF²μν ===

The coupling source term integrated over the BST composite volume:

:<math>\int_V S_{\rm device}\,d^3x = \alpha\int_V \varepsilon_{\rm eff}(V(t))\,E^2_{\rm bifilar}(\mathbf{x})\,d^3x</math>

For the [[Psi Stabilizer]], the objective is minimum variance in this integral over the drive cycle — steady ψ source rather than pulsed. The [[Shepard Tone Synthesis]] (D2) waveform is designed to achieve this. From D2's analysis, the minimum-variance condition requires the three Shepard carriers to have phase offsets of <math>T_{\rm sweep}/3</math> between them, which produces a flat temporal profile of <math>E^2(t)</math> and therefore a flat <math>F_{\mu\nu}F^{\mu\nu}(t)</math>.

=== Back-EMF Detection Mode ===

When the [[Anchor Controller]] (D6) switches the bifilar coil from drive mode to receive mode, the same coil functions as a [[ψ Detector]] (C10) via the reverse transduction path. A changing ψ field perturbs <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff}(t)</math> of the BST composite, which modulates the inter-trace capacitance, which induces a back-EMF:

:<math>V_{\rm bEMF} \propto \frac{d\varepsilon_{\rm eff}}{dt} \propto \frac{d\psi}{dt} = \rho_\psi</math>

The back-EMF is proportional to the ψ charge density (from [[ψ Conservation Laws]] A2). A lock-in amplifier referenced to the resonant frequency <math>\omega_{010}</math> extracts this signal from the thermal noise floor. Estimated sensitivity with lock-in at 1 Hz bandwidth: the back-EMF signal is detectable when <math>V_{\rm bEMF} > V_{\rm noise} = \sqrt{4k_BT\Delta f R} = \sqrt{4 \times 1.38\times10^{-23} \times 300 \times 1 \times 3} \approx 7\,\text{nV}</math> — setting the minimum detectable ψ charge density as a TML-3 measurement target.

== TML Measurement Protocol ==

=== TML-1: Trace Geometry Verification ===

After DLP printing and before composite infusion:
# Optical microscopy (calibrated stage, ×50 objective): measure trace width and gap at 10 locations across shell surface. Target: <math>w_{\rm trace} = 0.30 \pm 0.02</math> mm; <math>d_{\rm gap} = 0.20 \pm 0.02</math> mm.
# Four-point resistance measurement: measure resistance across each bifilar trace. Target: 1–4 Ω per trace.
# HiPot test: apply 400V DC between traces for 60 seconds. Zero leakage current (< 1 μA). Confirms dielectric overcoat integrity.

=== TML-2: Electromagnetic Compliance ===

After full shell assembly with composite fill and drive electronics:
# Near-field E-field scan: Langer EMV RF-B3 probe on 5 mm × 5 mm grid over shell outer surface. Drive at 40 kHz, 200V, 0.1% duty cycle. Map E-field distribution; compare against COMSOL prediction. Target: agreement to ±20% RMS.
# Far-field E at 10 cm: calibrated electric field probe (Narda SRM-3006 or equivalent). Drive at 40 kHz, 200V. Target: < 83 V/m at all azimuthal angles.
# Far-field B at 10 cm: three-axis calibrated magnetometer (Bartington Mag-03). Drive at 40 kHz, 200V. Target: < 27 μT at all azimuthal angles.
# Overlap integral verification: from measured E-field map and COMSOL ψ₀₁₀ mode, compute <math>\eta_{\rm overlap}</math>. Target: > 0.80.

